WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.420
<v Human Services Supervisor>I keep thinking about that session. The parent asked who

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.840
<v Human Services Supervisor>could see their name. I said DHS is here to

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.208
<v Human Services Supervisor>help. I meant it.

00:00:08.558 --> 00:00:11.020
<v Program Consultant>I know you did. But that was not what they

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.482
<v Program Consultant>asked. They asked who could see it. We did not

00:00:13.482 --> 00:00:15.206
<v Program Consultant>know the answer, and they could tell.

00:00:15.556 --> 00:00:18.586
<v Human Services Supervisor>Fair. I just did not want to scare anyone off

00:00:18.586 --> 00:00:20.404
<v Human Services Supervisor>by saying I was not sure.

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:24.354
<v Program Consultant>There is research on this. Across the US and thirty-three

00:00:24.354 --> 00:00:27.954
<v Program Consultant>other countries, fair process predicted trust in civil servants more

00:00:27.954 --> 00:00:31.554
<v Program Consultant>than outcomes did. Sometimes several times more. Saying I do

00:00:31.554 --> 00:00:35.154
<v Program Consultant>not know yet, here is when I will tell you,

00:00:35.154 --> 00:00:36.234
<v Program Consultant>is fair process.

00:00:36.584 --> 00:00:41.854
<v Human Services Supervisor>And people have reasons to ask. Minnesota apologized in 2010

00:00:41.854 --> 00:00:47.125
<v Human Services Supervisor>for what happened in state institutions. Unpaid labor. Procedures without

00:00:47.125 --> 00:00:49.760
<v Human Services Supervisor>consent. Graves with only numbers.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:54.132
<v Program Consultant>Right. And fear spreads past the people a rule covers.

00:00:54.132 --> 00:00:58.154
<v Program Consultant>In 2018, even some families where everyone born abroad was

00:00:58.154 --> 00:01:02.175
<v Program Consultant>already a citizen avoided benefits. They had nothing to lose

00:01:02.175 --> 00:01:03.382
<v Program Consultant>under that rule.

00:01:03.732 --> 00:01:06.818
<v Human Services Supervisor>So the answer matters more than the welcome. What do

00:01:06.818 --> 00:01:08.052
<v Human Services Supervisor>we do next time?

00:01:08.402 --> 00:01:11.669
<v Program Consultant>Tell people signing in is not needed for information. Get

00:01:11.669 --> 00:01:14.936
<v Program Consultant>the real answer on access from the area responsible for

00:01:14.936 --> 00:01:18.203
<v Program Consultant>data privacy. Send it in writing by a date we

00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:18.530
<v Program Consultant>name.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.800
<v Human Services Supervisor>Different topic, same skill. A staff member wants to report

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.720
<v Human Services Supervisor>a family because an uncle manages his niece's money. They

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:28.288
<v Human Services Supervisor>say it is tradition.

00:01:28.638 --> 00:01:31.542
<v Program Consultant>What did the staff member actually see or hear?

00:01:31.892 --> 00:01:35.712
<v Human Services Supervisor>The arrangement. And the niece said she cannot buy her

00:01:35.712 --> 00:01:36.476
<v Human Services Supervisor>own medicine.

00:01:36.826 --> 00:01:40.160
<v Program Consultant>Then those are two different things. The tradition alone is

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.495
<v Program Consultant>not a reason to report. Her statement about medicine might

00:01:43.495 --> 00:01:46.162
<v Program Consultant>be reason to believe she is being harmed.

00:01:46.512 --> 00:01:49.783
<v Human Services Supervisor>And if it is reason to believe, the statute says

00:01:49.783 --> 00:01:53.054
<v Human Services Supervisor>immediately. Not after a second visit. I will make sure

00:01:53.054 --> 00:01:56.325
<v Human Services Supervisor>the report goes in today, and talk with the staff

00:01:56.325 --> 00:01:57.960
<v Human Services Supervisor>member about what they noticed.
